  "_readme": "Copy this file to <id>.json, fill it in, then add a matching entry to data/manifest.json. Every player-facing string may be either a plain string or an {\"en\": ..., \"nl\": ..., \"fr\": ...} pair. Delete the pieces you do not need — the sidebar, the progress bar and the unlock order all follow this array.",

  "_refs": "Any row in any document may carry a \"ref\" (FR-01, DG-04, IV-02 — the prefix is yours to choose, it only has to be unique inside the case). Those references are the case's currency: the player cites them to rule a suspect out and to disprove a statement in an interview. A reference only becomes citable once the player has actually read the document it sits in, so a sealed file is never proof. A document with no refs is still readable, it just cannot be cited.",

  "_verdict": "Every innocent suspect needs a \"clearedBy\" array listing the refs that rule them out — citing any one of them is enough. The culprit gets \"clearedBy\": [], which is what makes them impossible to clear. Naming a suspect without clearing anyone is still allowed and still a gamble; clearing is how the player earns the answer instead of guessing it.",

